  "prompt": "Product wants the spread of session lengths. Use every app event in the data. A user's first app event starts a session, and an event more than 30 minutes after the same user's previous event starts a new one; an event exactly 30 minutes later stays in the same session. Measure each gap as the time between the two moments in event_ts, a UTC instant, never between clock times. A session's length is the time from its first to its last event. Put each session in one band: 'under 10' (less than 10 minutes, a one-event session included), '10 to 30' (10 minutes up to but not including 30), '30 to 60' (30 up to but not including 60) or '60 or more'. Return two columns, in this order: length_band and sessions. Return one row for each band that holds at least one session. Any row order is fine.",
  "output_contract": {
    "columns": [
      {
        "name": "length_band",
        "type_class": "text"
      },
      {
        "name": "sessions",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      }
    ],
    "grain": null
  },
